{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1399500-do-you-typically-play-characters-of-the-same-gender-and-age-as-yourself","id":1399500,"title":"Do you typically play characters of the same gender and age as yourself?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-06-27T21:31:47-07:00","id":1399500,"title":"Do you typically play characters of the same gender and age as yourself?","content":"I typically play female characters (though I have had a couple male PCs), but I like to mix up the ages of my characters a lot.<br /> <br /> For V:tM and V:tR, by \u201cage\u201d I mean the age you were Embraced.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T21:36:05-07:00","id":1399502,"title":"","content":"Played enough girls that I wondered if there might be a reason why. Figured it out at 21 <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T22:41:44-07:00","id":1399513,"title":"","content":"No. Obviously when Storytelling I play a wide range of characters. As a player I tend to go 50/50 my gender or something else, though that's more new. Ages all over the board, tend towards young.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-28-2020, 02:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T23:57:38-07:00","id":1399521,"title":"","content":"I like to play shapeshifters, of various kinds, where I'm cis <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bear_(gay_culture)\" target=\"_blank\">bisex </a><a href=\"https://pl.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gay_bear\" target=\"_blank\">bear</a> man. So... kinda not? Kinda yes? I just like shapeshifting, where I'm cis on day-to-day basis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T01:30:39-07:00","id":1399532,"title":"","content":"Ages can be all over the place from kids to old age. Never generated a female character though, played them as npcs when i gm, but never had any interest in a long-term character.<br /> <br /> I can only think of two people I've played with that actually played a character that wasn't the same sex as them","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Prone to being a Classic Curmudgeon, goshdarned whippersnappers...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1037-jamiemalk","name":"jamiemalk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1037_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T02:58:54-07:00","id":1399539,"title":"","content":"Awesome!!! Thanks for answering.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T03:07:29-07:00","id":1399544,"title":"","content":"I typically play characters that share my gender, but not exclusively. Age I tend to jump around a lot more on, though I find a lot of RPGs orient towards starting ages of 20-30 (or equivalent for non-humans). Either as established enough to be competent but still young enough for a lot of potential room for growth, or for game where characters tend to live a very long time, they tend to stop aging (or have it stopped) in their physical prime.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T03:14:58-07:00","id":1399547,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> In Dungeons and Dragons most of my characters and the characters of people I\u2019ve played with have been in their late teens to mid-twenties (or the equivalent for nonhumans). For WoD and Trinity Continuum the age range has been more diverse.<br /> <br /> I think people usually play the gender they feel most comfortable with. I prefer female characters, but I\u2019ve had two male PCs, once when we were all just goofing around and once in a more serious long-term campaign.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T04:22:40-07:00","id":1399559,"title":"","content":"I think there is a contextual element.<br /> <br /> IME one-shot con games, and certain styles of online play seem to be much more likely to have people playing farther from their personal identities. Con one-shots tend to mean being handed a pre-gen sheet and doing your best to run with the notes you get, so nobody's feeling too self conscious about how well they're doing. A forum PbP game means you only have to try to convey things via text; nobody is expecting you to try to match accents, inflections, and other affectations to help get into character even if it isn't serious acting.<br /> <br /> One of the things I definitely had to get over when I shifted from player to GM, was my nervousness about playing characters I simply can't act out in any meaningful way. When I was me, playing another teen white guy, they sounded authentic to me because I was playing something close enough to me that I felt it sounded right. Playing a 20 something looking actually over 100 year old female vampire that immigrated from China to the US, and having her sound like me? It felt exceedingly inauthentic because wtf did I know about sounding like someone with that experience? She just sounded like me (or worse me doing really bad voice work). As a GM, I'm never going to be someone who's NPCs are memorable because of my acting chops, so I know I need to put in my work on making them have moments in other forms. But I think this is something that probably impacts a lot of people.<br /> <br /> When you take away the pressure of live performance of characters, i've seen people far more willing to try things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T04:36:27-07:00","id":1399560,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> I totally understand.<br /> <br /> Both of my male characters I created myself (not pregens). One, Liam O\u2019Rourke of House Leanhaun, I took a lot of time creating and I played him over the course of several months. The other was a half-ogre barbarian named Zorg who liked to kill stuff and get laid a lot. I basically played him for shits and giggles over the course of a weekend with my friends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-01T03:58:43-07:00","id":1400275,"title":"","content":"If playing in person, I'm 95% likely to play as male. The exception is the handful of times I've had one whose personality was directly based off a fictional character I was able to mimic moderately well. (Rarity from MLP works surprisingly well as both Glass Walker and Etherite.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-01T07:39:25-07:00","id":1400310,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m about 60/40 gender-wise, leaning toward playing women though I\u2019m a man. Age is all over the map, though I think 20\u2019s are most common. Most of my games have been by text, which does make it easier .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-01T08:09:16-07:00","id":1400314,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12890_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12890\" data-vbnamecard=\"12890\">No One of Consequence</a>,@Dex Davican cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-01T09:59:12-07:00","id":1400336,"title":"","content":"As a genderfluid person, it\u2019s kind of a shrodinger\u2019s cat situation as to whether or not any given character I play is the same gender as me. But I play characters of genders and ages across the board.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-01T10:47:28-07:00","id":1400347,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a> awesome! \ud83d\ude0a","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-22T12:31:14-07:00","id":1479310,"title":"","content":"I normally play characters that are male and are usually look my age. In my case mid 40's and in regards to VTM &amp; VTR I was playing characters that were embraced in the 1800's and my eldest Changeling The Lost Character was taken in 1900 and returned in 1920 or so and appears to be in his late 50's currently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-23T12:17:52-07:00","id":1479361,"title":"","content":"Hm, I've now realized that I've never played an actual female character of my own (I don't count NPCs portrayed while acting as an ST), but I guess it never occurred to me to even want to. Usually my own characters are either androgynous, or monstrous, so it's not something that comes up. Last time someone asked me if my character might be into someone I rolled a die to randomly see if they had a preference other and Ace/Aro.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-30T21:28:24-07:00","id":1479863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1399500-do-you-typically-play-characters-of-the-same-gender-and-age-as-yourself?p=1399502#post1399502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Played enough girls that I wondered if there might be a reason why. Figured it out at 21 <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>This, but took me a while longer.<br /> <br /> But I had a variety of chars. It actually took one character of mine changing sex due to a magical curse during a D&amp;D campaign for me to begging playing females. I have a tendency to prefer young characters because I like the sense of a relatively fresh slate, but with time I did a number of characters of other ages, too, and I try to go for other ethnicities with some frequency.<br /> <br /> For the last years, though, I'm the ST too frequently, so not many characters of my own. I think the most recent one was for a L5R game, so young and Fake-Japanese because that's the game's standard anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-20T04:12:37-07:00","id":1484496,"title":"","content":"I don't have a proper overview, but guess I play about 50/50, with periods of playing a lot more female characters than male. Partly to liven up the roleplaying experience after only playing dudes for the first decade of my tenure, and partly because female fictional characters tend to be thin as paper and boring and/or predictable as hell, even and especially these days, and it's refreshing to get to do it right yourself and write and play a woman with something resembling depth and passion. Sans silly stereotypes, Mary Sueness or ridiculous overcompensation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27456-mr-sharp","name":"Mr Sharp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-12T16:42:20-07:00","id":1517843,"title":"","content":"I've usually played young guys and still do but tbh, I've played female characters too (my first RPG character ever was a girl) and I've played an elderly character before in long-running a campaign.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-13T09:29:52-07:00","id":1517882,"title":"","content":"I only played a female character once or twice who was a mage that was chasing her insane half brother all across the universe and feeling sad and terrified by his actions and remembering the child he was that she looked after as they were closer in age. It's was partly inspired by the Batman &amp; Joker relationship only with a family twist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-13T19:47:22-07:00","id":1517908,"title":"","content":"I stick to my gender and age. I was more willing to step outside those boxes when I was younger, but these days I'm self-conscious about age in particular, since the cultural touchstones are moving by so much faster. Like, can I imagine what it's like to play someone who's never known the Internet? Or the Simpsons? I feel like the artifice would be too obvious, like when Stephen King writes teenage characters and has to keep mentioning that they only watch TCM movies to explain why all their references are so dated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-14T00:24:07-07:00","id":1517924,"title":"","content":"I sometimes veer away from my age, though I stick to it nine times out of ten.<br /> I'm comfortable enough playing male or female (which is just as well, because STing a games that only ever feature one gender in it would be strange), though I think I prefer designing female characters and actually playing male characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-14T01:49:00-07:00","id":1517928,"title":"","content":"I guess its depends from game which I play. I guess it depends on the game I play. My favourite gaming series is Marvel. Playing Marvel games on <a href=\"https://pandoraboxarcade.com/official-pandora-arcade-split-console\" target=\"_blank\">Pandora Box Arcade Stick\u200b</a> consoles is an absolute blast! Imagine stepping into the shoes of your favorite superheroes and unleashing their incredible powers right at your fingertips. These consoles offer an extensive collection of Marvel games, from classic titles like X-Men and Avengers to modern hits like Marvel vs. Capcom. The immersive gameplay, stunning graphics, and epic storylines make for an unforgettable gaming experience. Whether you're battling villains as Iron Man, swinging through the city as Spider-Man, or teaming up with fellow heroes in intense multiplayer battles, Pandora Arcade consoles bring the Marvel universe to life like never before. Get ready to embark on thrilling adventures and save the world alongside your beloved Marvel characters. It's a must-try for any Marvel fan and gaming enthusiast!\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27939,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27939-dazert1","user":"Dazert1","date":". 07-17-2023, 08:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27939-dazert1","name":"Dazert1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27939_1.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-14T08:45:15-07:00","id":1517945,"title":"","content":"In regards to the age of the characters in any game. I try to keep it as close to my real life age as possible as I find the generation gap get more notable with each year and some the terminology they use is alien to me. I wouldn't know how to write a teenage character all that well anymore as whatever feelings I had at that point in my life are not as strong and my job and life experiences are more nuauced then say it was at age 15.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-14T11:09:48-07:00","id":1517962,"title":"","content":"I've played characters of multiple ages, genders, backgrounds, and ethnicities but the one weirdest part of all is that I've never played a Black character, despite being half-Black myself. Not against playing a character obviously but I just never really thought up of a Black character yet.<br /> <br /> I do wonder if that's because I always identified a bit more with my Scots-Irish roots from my Dad's side (his family were a mix of Scots-Irish and Romani) since my Dad and his family were the ones who raised me (my Mom died when I was two years old) along with my stepmom and her family (they're a mix of Italian and German)<br /> <br /> I'm gonna try to think of some new character ideas for an upcoming V20 game I've been invited to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":25920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","user":"Matt Corleone","date":". 07-14-2023, 02:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-14T13:45:09-07:00","id":1517975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1399500-do-you-typically-play-characters-of-the-same-gender-and-age-as-yourself?p=1517908#post1517908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I stick to my gender and age. I was more willing to step outside those boxes when I was younger, but these days I'm self-conscious about age in particular, since the cultural touchstones are moving by so much faster. Like, can I imagine what it's like to play someone who's never known the Internet? Or the Simpsons? I feel like the artifice would be too obvious, like when Stephen King writes teenage characters and has to keep mentioning that they only watch TCM movies to explain why all their references are so dated.</div> </div> </div> </div>While not to get too tangential here, I feel like this is one of the reasons why purely fictional settings are so popular in RPGs. You don't have to keep up with trends to a play a teenager in D&amp;D, or know about things that happened 60 years ago to play an old fart in Traveler. Even if it isn't canon to a given game, in a high fantasy setting, you can play with gender norms enough where Dragonblooded have fairly unified mannerisms from their dynastic and militaristic culture that focuses far more on class than gender in how people are expected to behave, speak, dress, and so on. You cut out a lot of these worries when you're not trying to do something close to the real world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-14T16:24:56-07:00","id":1517988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1399500-do-you-typically-play-characters-of-the-same-gender-and-age-as-yourself?p=1517975#post1517975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While not to get too tangential here,</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like your reply was relevant, if we're taking a poll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T10:03:12-07:00","id":1518047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1399500-do-you-typically-play-characters-of-the-same-gender-and-age-as-yourself?p=1517962#post1517962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've played characters of multiple ages, genders, backgrounds, and ethnicities but the one weirdest part of all is that I've never played a Black character, despite being half-Black myself. Not against playing a character obviously but I just never really thought up of a Black character yet.<br /> <br /> I do wonder if that's because I always identified a bit more with my Scots-Irish roots from my Dad's side (his family were a mix of Scots-Irish and Romani) since my Dad and his family were the ones who raised me (my Mom died when I was two years old) along with my stepmom and her family (they're a mix of Italian and German)<br /> <br /> I'm gonna try to think of some new character ideas for an upcoming V20 game I've been invited to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Irish and Spainish on my Mom Side and I did play up on those roots in a few characters I have played over the years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T10:09:45-07:00","id":1518050,"title":"","content":"That is a good point about it being easier to play a teenager in much older settings such as D&amp;D or related settings Heavy Arms. But I still prefer to play characters that are close to my age or just slightly older or younger as a preference. One exception would be playing Elves as what would be considered middle age or elderly for humans would be viewed as being an teenager or a young adult. Yes I played lots of elves in my time.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T13:02:33-07:00","id":1518066,"title":"","content":"I didn't mean to imply older settings even if two of my examples were definitely older ones (much older than Exalted which isn't a baby either), and there's a reason I picked both a fantasy and science fiction examples.. The applies equally well to more recent fantasy settings that keep the advantage of not trying to replicate real world cultures. Onyx Paths new The World Below will have the same advantage in being easier to RP away from your comfort zone as D&amp;D, as does something like Lancer from Massif Press.<br /> <br /> There's also games like Kids on Bikes or Masks where age is less of an option, but there's more room to play around with other dials. Kids on Bikes is meant to be set when the players were kids (or at least try since you can have a fairly mixed group) so that everyone has a more shared idea of references and so on. Masks also focuses on younger characters, but as team of super-teens, you can do things like be an alien who doesn't get Earth cultural stuff, or be raised from childhood by an established hero in a not so health fashion that leaves you very out of touch with normal kids your age when you finally leave to join your own team, etc.<br /> <br /> There are certainly ways games and influence us away from our normal pick (which I'm prone to as well as I play a lot of games that don't do much to push you away from that if you don't want to).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T13:09:20-07:00","id":1518069,"title":"","content":"It's definitely something I will keep in mind for future characters Heavy Arms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-17T19:43:58-07:00","id":1532793,"title":"","content":"I tend to play my own gender and near my age. Except, when I'm playing a mummy. For running vampire-games, I tend to play an elder-vampire, like an elder, not like a neonate that was embraced yesterday. I honestly think Antonio Banderas did a good job in Interview with the Vampire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-18T16:56:53-07:00","id":1532825,"title":"","content":"I don't care what people say about Tom Cruise in the movie at all. He was a great Lestat and captured the mood of the first book very well. In regards to playing immortals I usually stick around the 100-250 year mark as it suites my personal tastes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-20T11:39:36-07:00","id":1532915,"title":"","content":"Now the follow up to the Interview With A Vampire movie was really bad and didn't capture the mood of the series as we learn how the undead came to be made.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-20T16:35:16-07:00","id":1532926,"title":"","content":"As for running Vampire-games, I tend to start out all the PCs as mortal, and they are literally playing a historical-RPG, with a supernatural-twist. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1399500-do-you-typically-play-characters-of-the-same-gender-and-age-as-yourself?p=1532825#post1532825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't care what people say about Tom Cruise in the movie at all. He was a great Lestat and captured the mood of the first book very well. In regards to playing immortals I usually stick around the 100-250 year mark as it suites my personal tastes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Tom Cruise is a good Lestat; however, Sam Reid was a better Lestat; he captured the essence of the character from the books better. <br /> <br /> tQotD, movie, was just that, a movie. It wasn't great, but it could have been a lot worse and it had a few good gems in it. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\u2615","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-06T12:42:39-07:00","id":1533715,"title":"","content":"True the Dracula 2000 series of films were pretty bad and I do like Mr. Butler and the late Rutger Hauer as actors and they were not enough to save the series.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-06T15:04:49-07:00","id":1533723,"title":"","content":"I liked Dracula 2000 and the Queen of the Damned movie unironically. Same goes for the first two Blade movies.<br /> <br /> There, I said it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-06T15:21:07-07:00","id":1533724,"title":"","content":"The first Dracula 2000 movie was decent fare, but the following films in the series was bad and I did enjoy the first two Blade movies but didn't feel a desire to see the third one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-06T21:38:00-07:00","id":1533735,"title":"","content":"Don't hate me but I did enjoy Indiana Jones and The Temple Of The Crystal Skull. To me it was a fun movie that did its job well and sure it wasn't as good as the first 3, but I went with the idea of the fans having to high of an expectation given that they had to move forward in time to reflect an older Harrison Ford.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-06T23:29:05-07:00","id":1533737,"title":"","content":"I just go here cause I have notifications - Have we gone too far off topic here <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27361_11.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27361\" data-vbnamecard=\"27361\">Lysander</a> &amp; <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25920_8.webp');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25920\" data-vbnamecard=\"25920\">Matt Corleone</a> ? Maybe start a new one about movies?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-07T09:25:51-07:00","id":1533754,"title":"","content":"Fair enough Wyrdhammer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-13T09:31:52-07:00","id":1537309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1399500-do-you-typically-play-characters-of-the-same-gender-and-age-as-yourself?p=1399544#post1399544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I typically play characters that share my gender, but not exclusively. Age I tend to jump around a lot more on, though I find a lot of RPGs orient towards starting ages of 20-30 (or equivalent for non-humans). Either as established enough to be competent but still young enough for a lot of potential room for growth, or for game where characters tend to live a very long time, they tend to stop aging (or have it stopped) in their physical prime.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's some pretty interesting information.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28525,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28525-weswinnefred","user":"weswinnefred","date":". 06-13-2024, 12:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28525-weswinnefred","name":"weswinnefred","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28525_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-19T21:02:57-07:00","id":1537671,"title":"","content":"I had a player that insisted on playing only female-characters and wanted to be a tank-crewman in a World War 2, mortals-game based on the Eastern Front; I told him there were no women in the German army as a tank-gunner. I wanted to be historically accurate; I only allowed it after I first saw <i>Europa, Europa</i> and it gave me an idea: I told him he had to have his character masquerade as a guy. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1399500-do-you-typically-play-characters-of-the-same-gender-and-age-as-yourself?p=1533715#post1533715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True the Dracula 2000 series of films were pretty bad and I do like Mr. Butler and the late Rutger Hauer as actors and they were not enough to save the series.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it was John Carpenter's what ever that was mediocre.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-20T11:19:34-07:00","id":1537718,"title":"","content":"That level of &quot;historical accuracy&quot; always feels weird to insist on. By '43 the German army had relented to the demands for more troops and softened it's stances on an all-male military. There weren't (openly) any women tank-gunners. But the German anti-aircraft gun battalions became fully integrated, so thousands of German women were part of gun crews by that point in the war (as well as a number of non-combat units like women taking over nearly all of the non-combat piloting roles because Hitler was obsessed with women not firing weapon more than he was with them not serving in the military). And while the war ended before it mattered, as it went on, even Hitler finally relented and signed off starting full integration of women into German's military forces as the Allies were starting to encircle Germany.<br /> <br /> It is such a small deviation from history, and a big deal for the player's fun. I'm glad if everyone was happy with a compromise reached, but these sorts of appeals to historical accuracy always ring really hollow to me because I've never seen a historical game that's ever that consistently accurate (and of course history is also always a bit vague because history is full of holes and biases).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-20T17:48:21-07:00","id":1537734,"title":"","content":"I'm drawing a blank on what vampire movie did John Carpenter do, but outside from Escape from New York I'm never watched much of his stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-05T00:38:58-07:00","id":1559228,"title":"","content":"With each passing birthday, my MC's starting age becomes 1 year older.<br /> <br /> It's how I maintain the sense of an escapist fantasy.<br /> <br /> I'm not old! You're old! Shut up!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-05T22:49:54-07:00","id":1559238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1399500-do-you-typically-play-characters-of-the-same-gender-and-age-as-yourself?p=1537734#post1537734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm drawing a blank on what vampire movie did John Carpenter do, but outside from Escape from New York I'm never watched much of his stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was literally just called <i>'Vampires'</i> and had 2 direct to video sequels.<br /> <br /> <i>Vampires:</i> Los Muertos.<br /> <br /> <i>Vampires:</i> The Turning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"l